{"title":"MRI Technologist Roadmap","role":"MRI Technologist","summary":"An MRI Technologist operates MRI equipment and supports radiologists and clinical teams in obtaining high-quality diagnostic images. The role combines patient preparation, MRI safety, positioning, protocol execution, image acquisition, contrast-related workflow, equipment operation, quality control, and patient care.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Medical Imaging Technology - MRI / CT Specialisation"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"An MRI Technologist operates MRI equipment and supports radiologists and clinical teams in obtaining high-quality diagnostic images. The role combines patient preparation, MRI safety, positioning, protocol execution, image acquisition, contrast-related workflow, equipment operation, quality control, and patient care."},{"type":"p","text":"MRI is particularly important for imaging:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Brain and spine"},{"text":"Joints and musculoskeletal structures"},{"text":"Abdomen and pelvis"},{"text":"Blood vessels"},{"text":"Cardiac structures"},{"text":"Soft tissues"},{"text":"Tumours and other pathological conditions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Typical workplaces include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Multispecialty hospitals"},{"text":"Diagnostic imaging centres"},{"text":"Radiology departments"},{"text":"Cancer centres"},{"text":"Neuroscience hospitals"},{"text":"Orthopaedic centres"},{"text":"Emergency hospitals"},{"text":"Medical colleges"},{"text":"Research and advanced imaging centres"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"Exact scope of practice, credentialing, registration, contrast-related responsibilities, and permitted duties depend on the recognized qualification, institution, employer, equipment, supervision, and applicable regulations."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Career Stage","Possible Roles"],"rows":[[{"text":"Entry Level"},{"text":"MRI Technologist, MRI Technician, Radiology Technologist"}],[{"text":"1–3 Years"},{"text":"Experienced MRI Technologist"}],[{"text":"3–6 Years"},{"text":"Senior MRI Technologist"}],[{"text":"5–8 Years"},{"text":"MRI/Imaging Supervisor"}],[{"text":"Advanced"},{"text":"MRI Application Specialist"}],[{"text":"Specialized"},{"text":"Advanced MRI Technologist"}],[{"text":"Management"},{"text":"Imaging Department Coordinator / Manager"}],[{"text":"Industry"},{"text":"MRI Clinical Application Specialist"}],[{"text":"Research"},{"text":"Medical Imaging Research Assistant"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During the Degree","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Imaging & Healthcare Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong fundamentals in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human anatomy"},{"text":"Human physiology"},{"text":"Basic pathology"},{"text":"Medical terminology"},{"text":"Patient care"},{"text":"Radiographic principles"},{"text":"Medical imaging fundamentals"},{"text":"Physics fundamentals"},{"text":"Healthcare ethics"},{"text":"Infection prevention"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Pay particular attention to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Brain anatomy"},{"text":"Spine"},{"text":"Musculoskeletal anatomy"},{"text":"Thorax"},{"text":"Abdomen"},{"text":"Pelvis"},{"text":"Vascular anatomy"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A strong anatomical understanding is essential for selecting appropriate imaging positions and recognizing whether images adequately cover the requested anatomy."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — MRI Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MRI principles"},{"text":"Magnetic fields"},{"text":"Radiofrequency pulses"},{"text":"Nuclear magnetic resonance"},{"text":"T1/T2 relaxation"},{"text":"Proton density"},{"text":"Signal generation"},{"text":"Spatial encoding"},{"text":"Gradients"},{"text":"Coils"},{"text":"MRI sequences"},{"text":"Image orientation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Axial"},{"text":"Sagittal"},{"text":"Coronal"},{"text":"Oblique planes"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3/4 — Advanced MRI Practice"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop practical exposure to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient screening"},{"text":"MRI safety"},{"text":"Patient positioning"},{"text":"Coil selection"},{"text":"Protocol selection"},{"text":"Sequence planning"},{"text":"Image acquisition"},{"text":"Contrast-enhanced MRI workflows"},{"text":"Motion reduction"},{"text":"Image quality control"},{"text":"Emergency procedures"},{"text":"Equipment troubleshooting"},{"text":"Digital image management"}]},{"type":"h","text":"MRI Workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Imaging Request","Patient Identification","Clinical History Verification","MRI Safety Screening","Contraindication / Implant Assessment","Patient Preparation","Coil Selection","Patient Positioning","Protocol Selection","Sequence Acquisition","Image Quality Check","Additional Sequences if Required","Post-Procedure Patient Care","Image Transfer / PACS","Radiologist Interpretation"]},{"type":"p","text":"The technologist's role is to produce technically appropriate images and support patient safety; diagnostic interpretation is performed by the appropriately qualified radiologist/clinician."},{"type":"h","text":"Core MRI Skills"},{"type":"table","header":["Skill Area","What to Learn"],"rows":[[{"text":"MRI Physics"},{"text":"NMR, relaxation, signal generation"}],[{"text":"Safety"},{"text":"Magnetic-field hazards and screening"}],[{"text":"Positioning"},{"text":"Accurate patient positioning"}],[{"text":"Coils"},{"text":"Appropriate coil selection"}],[{"text":"Protocols"},{"text":"Sequence and parameter selection"}],[{"text":"Imaging"},{"text":"High-quality image acquisition"}],[{"text":"Contrast"},{"text":"Contrast-related workflow and safety"}],[{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Patient preparation and reassurance"}],[{"text":"Quality Control"},{"text":"Image quality assessment"}],[{"text":"PACS"},{"text":"Image transfer and management"}],[{"text":"Equipment"},{"text":"Basic operational troubleshooting"}],[{"text":"Emergency"},{"text":"MRI-specific emergency procedures"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"MRI Physics Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"A strong technologist should understand:"},{"type":"h","text":"Magnetic Field"},{"type":"p","text":"MRI uses a strong static magnetic field to align hydrogen nuclei."},{"type":"h","text":"Radiofrequency"},{"type":"p","text":"RF energy is used to manipulate the magnetization of the tissue."},{"type":"h","text":"Relaxation"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"T1 relaxation"},{"text":"T2 relaxation"},{"text":"T2* effects"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Spatial Encoding"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the role of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Gradient coils"},{"text":"Frequency encoding"},{"text":"Phase encoding"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Signal"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the relationship between:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Signal"},{"text":"Noise"},{"text":"Contrast"},{"text":"Resolution"},{"text":"Scan time"}]},{"type":"h","text":"MRI Sequences"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop familiarity with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"T1-weighted"},{"text":"T2-weighted"},{"text":"Proton-density"},{"text":"FLAIR"},{"text":"STIR"},{"text":"DWI"},{"text":"ADC"},{"text":"GRE"},{"text":"SWI"},{"text":"Fat-suppressed sequences"},{"text":"3D sequences"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The student should understand why a sequence is used and what type of tissue contrast it provides, rather than simply memorizing sequence names."},{"type":"h","text":"MRI Safety"},{"type":"p","text":"This is one of the most important competencies for an MRI Technologist."},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Static magnetic-field hazards"},{"text":"Projectile risk"},{"text":"RF heating"},{"text":"Burns"},{"text":"Acoustic noise"},{"text":"Implant screening"},{"text":"Device compatibility"},{"text":"Patient monitoring"},{"text":"Emergency procedures"},{"text":"MRI-zone concepts"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Safety Workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Patient Arrives","Identity Verification","MRI Safety Questionnaire","Implant / Device Screening","Metal Screening","Medical History Review","Safety Clearance","MRI Examination"]},{"type":"p","text":"Never assume an implant or device is MRI-safe without appropriate verification."},{"type":"h","text":"MRI Zones"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the concept of controlled MRI environments and restricted access."},{"type":"p","text":"The technologist should ensure that:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Unauthorized individuals do not enter restricted areas"},{"text":"Ferromagnetic objects are kept out"},{"text":"Screening is completed before entry"},{"text":"Emergency procedures are followed"},{"text":"Equipment is appropriately controlled"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Patient Preparation"},{"type":"p","text":"Before the scan:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Confirm identity"},{"text":"Verify examination"},{"text":"Review clinical information"},{"text":"Perform MRI safety screening"},{"text":"Explain procedure"},{"text":"Explain noise and scan duration"},{"text":"Provide hearing protection"},{"text":"Position patient"},{"text":"Select appropriate coil"},{"text":"Establish communication method"},{"text":"For anxious or claustrophobic patients, use appropriate communication and follow the department's established procedures."}]},{"type":"h","text":"MRI Contrast Awareness"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop foundational knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Contrast-enhanced MRI"},{"text":"Contrast administration workflow"},{"text":"Patient screening"},{"text":"Relevant renal-function considerations"},{"text":"Allergic/adverse reactions"},{"text":"IV access"},{"text":"Post-contrast observation"},{"text":"The technologist should work strictly according to institutional protocols and authorized clinical orders."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Image Quality"},{"type":"p","text":"A high-quality MRI study depends on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Correct Patient"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Correct Anatomy"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Correct Positioning"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Correct Coil"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Correct Protocol"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Correct Sequence"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Minimal Motion"},{"text":"+"}]},{"type":"flow","items":["Adequate Signal-to-Noise","Diagnostic-Quality Images"]},{"type":"p","text":"Monitor for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Motion artifacts"},{"text":"Aliasing"},{"text":"Susceptibility artifacts"},{"text":"Wrap-around"},{"text":"Chemical shift"},{"text":"Flow artifacts"},{"text":"Poor fat suppression"},{"text":"Inadequate signal"},{"text":"Incorrect positioning"}]},{"type":"h","text":"MRI Artifacts"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to recognize and troubleshoot:"},{"type":"h","text":"Motion Artifact"},{"type":"p","text":"Usually associated with patient movement."},{"type":"h","text":"Susceptibility Artifact"},{"type":"p","text":"Common around:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Metal"},{"text":"Air/tissue interfaces"},{"text":"Certain materials"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Chemical Shift"},{"type":"p","text":"Caused by differences in resonance frequencies of fat and water."},{"type":"h","text":"Aliasing"},{"type":"p","text":"Occurs when the field of view does not adequately cover the anatomy."},{"type":"h","text":"Flow Artifact"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Can occur due to moving blood or fluid."},{"text":"Understanding artifacts helps the technologist decide when image acquisition should be adjusted or repeated."}]},{"type":"h","text":"MRI Applications"},{"type":"h","text":"Neurological MRI"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn imaging workflows for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Brain"},{"text":"Spine"},{"text":"Cranial nerves"},{"text":"Stroke-related imaging"},{"text":"Tumour evaluation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Musculoskeletal MRI"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Knee"},{"text":"Shoulder"},{"text":"Hip"},{"text":"Ankle"},{"text":"Wrist"},{"text":"Sports injuries"},{"text":"Ligaments"},{"text":"Tendons"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Abdominal MRI"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Liver"},{"text":"Pancreas"},{"text":"Kidneys"},{"text":"Adrenal glands"},{"text":"Biliary system"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Pelvic MRI"},{"type":"p","text":"Exposure to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Prostate"},{"text":"Uterus"},{"text":"Ovaries"},{"text":"Rectum"},{"text":"Pelvic soft tissues"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Cardiovascular MRI"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop introductory awareness of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cardiac MRI"},{"text":"Angiography"},{"text":"Flow imaging"},{"text":"Vascular imaging"}]},{"type":"h","text":"CT Knowledge"},{"type":"p","text":"Because the specialization includes MRI / CT, maintain foundational CT knowledge even when targeting MRI."},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CT principles"},{"text":"X-ray generation"},{"text":"Detectors"},{"text":"Hounsfield units"},{"text":"CT reconstruction"},{"text":"Contrast-enhanced CT"},{"text":"Radiation safety"},{"text":"CT protocols"},{"text":"This gives the graduate flexibility across diagnostic-imaging departments."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation Safety"},{"type":"p","text":"MRI itself does not use ionizing radiation, but CT does."},{"type":"p","text":"Therefore, students working across MRI/CT departments should understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Radiation dose"},{"text":"ALARA principles"},{"text":"Shielding"},{"text":"Exposure optimization"},{"text":"Patient protection"},{"text":"Occupational safety"},{"text":"Never treat MRI and CT safety as the same concept."}]},{"type":"h","text":"PACS & Digital Imaging"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"PACS"},{"text":"DICOM"},{"text":"RIS"},{"text":"Electronic medical records"},{"text":"Image transfer"},{"text":"Study verification"},{"text":"Patient identification"},{"text":"Digital archiving"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Digital Workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["MRI Acquisition","Image Reconstruction","Quality Check","DICOM","PACS","Radiologist Workstation","Clinical Report"]},{"type":"h","text":"Equipment Knowledge"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the major MRI system components:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Main magnet"},{"text":"Gradient system"},{"text":"RF system"},{"text":"Patient table"},{"text":"RF coils"},{"text":"Console"},{"text":"Cooling system"},{"text":"Monitoring equipment"},{"text":"Emergency equipment"},{"text":"Learn basic troubleshooting, but do not perform unauthorized technical repairs."}]},{"type":"h","text":"AI & Advanced Imaging Technology"},{"type":"p","text":"MRI is increasingly incorporating:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI image reconstruction"},{"text":"Automated segmentation"},{"text":"Motion correction"},{"text":"Scan-time optimization"},{"text":"AI-based protocol assistance"},{"text":"Quantitative imaging"},{"text":"Automated image quality assessment"},{"text":"Radiomics"},{"text":"3D reconstruction"},{"text":"Advanced visualization"}]},{"type":"h","text":"AI-Assisted Workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["MRI Acquisition","AI Reconstruction / Enhancement","Image Quality Check","Technologist Review","PACS","Radiologist Interpretation"]},{"type":"p","text":"AI tools should be treated as assistive technology, with appropriate human quality and safety checks."},{"type":"h","text":"Final-Year Project Ideas"},{"type":"h","text":"Project 1"},{"type":"h","text":"Comparison of MRI Image Quality Across Different Acquisition Parameters"},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2"},{"type":"h","text":"Study of Common MRI Artifacts and Their Reduction Techniques"},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3"},{"type":"h","text":"Assessment of MRI Safety Awareness Among Patients and Healthcare Staff"},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4"},{"type":"h","text":"Optimization of MRI Workflow to Reduce Patient Waiting Time"},{"type":"h","text":"Project 5"},{"type":"h","text":"Analysis of Motion Artifacts in MRI and Techniques for Reduction"},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced Project"},{"type":"h","text":"AI-Assisted MRI Image Segmentation Using Deep Learning"}]},{"heading":"Internship Strategy","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Multispecialty hospitals"},{"text":"Diagnostic imaging centres"},{"text":"Neuroscience hospitals"},{"text":"Cancer centres"},{"text":"Orthopaedic hospitals"},{"text":"Medical colleges"},{"text":"Advanced radiology centres"},{"text":"Research imaging facilities"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Prioritize hands-on exposure to:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Patient Screening","MRI Safety","Positioning","Coil Selection","Protocol Setup","Sequence Acquisition","Image Quality Check","PACS Transfer","Patient Recovery"]}]},{"heading":"Entry-Level Career Options","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Possible roles include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MRI Technologist"},{"text":"MRI Technician"},{"text":"Radiology Technologist"},{"text":"CT/MRI Technologist"},{"text":"Diagnostic Imaging Technologist"},{"text":"MRI Department Technician"},{"text":"Imaging Centre Technologist"},{"text":"Advanced Imaging Assistant"},{"text":"Clinical Imaging Technician"},{"text":"Medical Imaging Application Trainee"},{"text":"Exact eligibility depends on the recognized qualification and employer requirements."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Employer Skill Matrix"},{"type":"table","header":["Employer","Most Valuable Skills"],"rows":[[{"text":"Multispecialty Hospital"},{"text":"MRI + patient care"}],[{"text":"Diagnostic Centre"},{"text":"Protocols + image quality"}],[{"text":"Cancer Centre"},{"text":"MRI + oncology imaging workflows"}],[{"text":"Neuroscience Centre"},{"text":"Neuro MRI"}],[{"text":"Orthopaedic Centre"},{"text":"Musculoskeletal MRI"}],[{"text":"Medical College"},{"text":"Imaging + academic knowledge"}],[{"text":"Research Centre"},{"text":"Advanced imaging + data"}],[{"text":"Equipment Manufacturer"},{"text":"MRI operation + technical communication"}]]}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Additional Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Useful areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MRI safety"},{"text":"Advanced MRI techniques"},{"text":"CT fundamentals"},{"text":"Radiation safety"},{"text":"Basic Life Support"},{"text":"Contrast safety"},{"text":"PACS/DICOM"},{"text":"Healthcare quality"},{"text":"Medical imaging informatics"},{"text":"Advanced anatomy"},{"text":"Image analysis"},{"text":"For certifications, verify that the provider and course are appropriate for the intended professional role."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Higher Education Options"},{"type":"p","text":"Depending on eligibility and available programs:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Sc. Medical Imaging Technology"},{"text":"M.Sc. Medical Radiology & Imaging Technology"},{"text":"M.Sc. Radiological Imaging"},{"text":"M.Sc. Medical Imaging"},{"text":"M.Sc. Healthcare Technology"},{"text":"M.Sc. Medical Physics — where eligibility permits"},{"text":"Healthcare Management"},{"text":"Hospital Administration"},{"text":"Medical Imaging Informatics"},{"text":"Clinical Research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Career Specializations"}]},{"heading":"Neuro MRI","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Brain"},{"text":"Spine"},{"text":"Stroke"},{"text":"Neurological disorders"},{"text":"Advanced neuroimaging"}]}]},{"heading":"Musculoskeletal MRI","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sports injuries"},{"text":"Joints"},{"text":"Ligaments"},{"text":"Tendons"},{"text":"Cartilage"}]}]},{"heading":"Abdominal & Pelvic MRI","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Liver"},{"text":"Pancreas"},{"text":"Pelvis"},{"text":"Prostate"},{"text":"Gynecological imaging"}]}]},{"heading":"Cardiac MRI","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cardiac anatomy"},{"text":"Functional imaging"},{"text":"Flow"},{"text":"Cardiovascular protocols"}]}]},{"heading":"MRI Application Specialist","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Work with medical imaging manufacturers to support:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"System implementation"},{"text":"Clinical applications"},{"text":"User training"},{"text":"Protocol optimization"}]}]},{"heading":"Imaging Informatics","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"PACS"},{"text":"DICOM"},{"text":"RIS"},{"text":"Image management"},{"text":"Healthcare IT"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["MRI Technologist","Senior MRI Technologist","Advanced MRI Technologist","MRI / Imaging Supervisor","Imaging Department Manager","Radiology Operations Manager"]},{"type":"h","text":"Medical-Device Industry Route"},{"type":"flow","items":["MRI Technologist","Clinical Application Specialist","Senior Application Specialist","Clinical Imaging Specialist","Regional Application Manager","Product / Clinical Management"]},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging Technologies"},{"type":"p","text":"The future MRI environment is increasingly moving toward:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI reconstruction"},{"text":"Faster MRI acquisition"},{"text":"Automated positioning"},{"text":"AI protocol optimization"},{"text":"Quantitative MRI"},{"text":"3D imaging"},{"text":"Functional MRI"},{"text":"Diffusion imaging"},{"text":"MR spectroscopy"},{"text":"Advanced cardiac imaging"},{"text":"MR angiography"},{"text":"Remote equipment monitoring"},{"text":"Imaging informatics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended Final Skill Stack"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human Anatomy"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"MRI Physics"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"MRI Safety"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Patient Care"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Patient Positioning"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Coil Selection"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"MRI Protocols"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Sequence Knowledge"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Image Quality"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Artifact Recognition"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Contrast Workflow"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"PACS / DICOM"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"CT Fundamentals"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Radiation Safety Awareness"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"AI / Advanced Imaging"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Target Profile by Graduation"},{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, the student should ideally be able to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Understand MRI physics fundamentals"},{"text":"Identify major MRI system components"},{"text":"Perform systematic MRI safety screening"},{"text":"Understand implant and device-safety considerations"},{"text":"Prepare and position patients appropriately"},{"text":"Select appropriate coils under departmental protocols"},{"text":"Understand major MRI sequences"},{"text":"Assist with routine MRI protocols"},{"text":"Recognize common image artifacts"},{"text":"Evaluate basic image quality"},{"text":"Understand contrast-related workflows"},{"text":"Follow emergency and patient-safety procedures"},{"text":"Work with PACS and DICOM systems"},{"text":"Understand CT fundamentals and radiation safety"},{"text":"Maintain accurate imaging documentation"},{"text":"Communicate effectively with patients and clinical teams"},{"text":"Understand AI-assisted imaging and modern MRI technologies"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Best Overall Positioning"},{"type":"flow","items":["“MRI Technologist with strong MRI safety","protocol execution","image-quality optimization","PACS/DICOM","CT fundamentals","advanced digital imaging skills.”"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"This positioning provides a strong foundation for employment in hospital radiology departments, diagnostic imaging centres, specialized MRI facilities, neuroscience and oncology centres, while creating longer-term pathways toward advanced MRI specialization, imaging informatics, department supervision, research, and medical-device clinical application roles."}]}]}